/**
 * Tools that deliberately have no MAIN BLOCK, each with the reason.
 *
 * A REFUSAL WITHOUT A REASON EXPIRES INTO A GAP. These are not oversights, and as of v3853 they are TWO
 * DIFFERENT REFUSALS, which the one-reason comment that stood here could not say:
 *
 *   (1) INJECTION -- the tool takes its corpus or its registry FROM THE CALLER, and a main block would have to
 *       invent one. Inventing it is how a tool starts disagreeing with the gate that uses it.
 *   (2) *** THE PAGE IS THE DOOR *** -- the module is imported by a BROWSER PAGE, so it may carry no `node:`
 *       specifier at all. A main block needs `import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href`, which
 *       needs node:url, and the Windows path law (v2759) forbids the string comparison that would avoid it.
 *       THERE IS NO MAIN BLOCK THAT DOES NOT COST THE FILE ITS PAGE.
 *
 * AND (2) IS NOT A LESSER DOOR. toolFrontDoor's own header says the standing preference is "a page, or a route
 * with an HTML front end"; these have exactly the form the rule prefers and lack only the CLI half.
 */

// *** v3853 -- THE CARRIED RED WAS NEVER "reconOps IS SILENT". IT WAS NINE FILES AND A TIMEOUT. ***
//
// The record named ONE of them. Fixing that one and re-running named EIGHT MORE, every one with the identical
// disposition -- which is why the red never shrank in the versions it was carried: the list was fixed at its
// first line and nobody read past it. MEASURED, not inferred: all nine carry ZERO `node:` imports (reconOps's
// only `node:` hit is a COMMENT explaining why its siblings have one), and every one is imported by a page.
//
// *** AND THE TREE HAD ALREADY DECIDED THIS, IN WRITING, THIRTY-FIVE VERSIONS AGO. *** statistical-mechanics.html
// says of itself: "Eight graded modules that had no door at all -- runnable only by typing a selfcheck path
// (seven found this page at v3818, the paramagnet at v3820)." THE DOOR WAS BUILT AND THIS REGISTRY WAS NEVER
// TOLD. That is section 3's own finding turned on this file -- THE SECOND COPY IS NEVER THE ONE THAT GETS
// UPDATED -- and the cost was a gate demanding a CLI from eight files that may not have one.

// *** AND THE (2) REASON NAMES A PAGE, WHICH MAKES IT A WIRING CLAIM -- SO IT IS DATA, NOT PROSE. ***
// "statistical-mechanics.html imports it" is a fact about the import graph, and toolFrontDoor's own section 3
// carries this tree's verdict on those: "A WIRING CLAIM IS A FACT ABOUT THE IMPORT GRAPH WRITTEN DOWN IN PROSE
// WHERE NOTHING RE-DERIVES IT (v3331-v3372, twelve instances), and ASK THE THING THAT WALKS." Writing nine such
// sentences and calling the red cleared would have been the twelve-instance defect, committed in the entry that
// quotes it. THE PAGE IS THEREFORE A FIELD: PAGE_DOOR below is derived from the same rows as the sentences, so
// the two cannot drift, and section 3 of the gate asks the RESOLVER whether that page really imports the file.
//
// ONE ROW, TWO VIEWS. Nine identical copy-pasted sentences would be the two-declarations defect as well; the
// per-module clause is the only part that actually differs.
const PAGE_DOOR_ROWS = [
    ["physics/md/maxwellSpeed.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the speed distribution whose v_p:<v>:v_rms ratios are a function of the dimension alone"],
    ["physics/thermal/blackbody.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the Planck shape and both Wien peaks, the pair whose ratio is 0.568 and not 1"],
    ["physics/thermal/debye.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the heat capacity at both ends -- Dulong-Petit above, the T^3 law below"],
    ["physics/thermal/bec.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the condensate fraction and the cusp at Tc"],
    ["physics/thermal/fermi.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the degenerate gas: Sommerfeld's linear C_V and the n^{5/3} pressure"],
    ["physics/thermal/sackurTetrode.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the classical entropy and the point where it announces its own death"],
    ["physics/thermal/chemicalPotential.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the panel the page's own description says to look at -- one density constraint, three fugacities"],
    ["physics/statmech/paramagnet.mjs", "statistical-mechanics.html",
     "draws the Schottky anomaly; it joined the other seven at v3820, two versions after the page was built"],
    ["physics/tomography/reconOps.mjs", "ct.html",
     "runs both backprojectors side by side -- and reconOps.mjs EXISTS PRECISELY TO HAVE NO node: IMPORTS, which reconOps-selfcheck asserts by name"],
];

/** rel -> the page that is its front door. THE CHECKABLE HALF of the (2) reason; the gate asks the resolver. */
export const PAGE_DOOR = new Map(PAGE_DOOR_ROWS.map(([rel, page]) => [rel, page]));

const pageIsTheDoor = (page, what) =>
    "THE PAGE IS THE DOOR: " + page + " imports it and " + what + ". NO `node:` imports, which is what lets a " +
    "browser resolve it -- and a main block needs node:url for the pathToFileURL comparison the Windows path " +
    "law requires, so the CLI half cannot be had without losing the page half. This rule prefers the page.";

export const NO_MAIN = new Map([
    ["tools/ship/boundaryLint.mjs",
     "exports scanBoundaries(src), a PER-FILE primitive: the corpus is the caller's choice, and picking one here would make the tool disagree with the gate that uses it"],
    ["tools/roundhouse/claimTrace.mjs",
     "claimTrace(engRoot, D, K) takes the device registry AND knobGate by injection -- a main block would have to choose them, which is exactly the coupling the injection exists to avoid"],
    // v3377 -- patchBase's entry WAS HERE AND IS DELETED, WHICH IS WHAT ITS OWN REASON INSTRUCTED: "WHEN
    // SOMEBODY BUILDS IT, THIS ENTRY GOES RED AND SHOULD BE DELETED, NOT WEAKENED." The door it named was
    // built -- sysadminBridge.patchScan() beside the Downloads scan, routed at /sys/patchbase, with a row in
    // System Tools. THE ANTIDOTE WORKED FOR THE THIRD TIME (v3196 wrote it, v3197 obeyed it, this is v3377).
    ...PAGE_DOOR_ROWS.map(([rel, page, what]) => [rel, pageIsTheDoor(page, what)]),
    ["tools/ship/controlDossier.mjs",
     "controlDossier(engRoot, census) consumes roundTripCensus's output: it reports ON a measurement rather than taking one, and roundTripCensus is offered above"],
]);

/** Exact-match only. A page may ask for a tool BY NAME and never by path, pattern or anything it composed. */
export function isReportingTool(rel) {
    return REPORTING.some((t) => t.rel === String(rel)) || ARTEFACT_TOOLS.some((t) => t.rel === String(rel));
}

/** The artefact row for a tool, or null. ITS ARGS COME FROM HERE AND NEVER FROM THE CALLER -- a route that took
 *  flags from a query string would be an arbitrary command runner wearing a tool's name, which is the same
 *  refusal gatesBridge makes about filenames. */
export function artefactTool(rel) {
    return ARTEFACT_TOOLS.find((t) => t.rel === String(rel)) || null;
}
